# Cheat Sheet

## Generated functions
{: .col-2}

### Struct factory (`deffactory user(params \\ %{}), struct: User`)

| Function                              | Returns                        |
| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| `build_user_struct/0,1,2`             | `%User{}`, not persisted       |
| `build_user_params/0,1,2`             | Clean params map (atom keys)   |
| `build_user_string_params/0,1,2`      | Clean params map (string keys) |
| `insert_user/0,1,2`                   | Inserted `%User{}`             |
| `insert_user_struct/1,2`              | Inserts an already-built struct |
| `build_user_struct_list/1,2,3`        | `[%User{}, ...]`               |
| `build_user_params_list/1,2,3`        | `[%{}, ...]`                   |
| `build_user_string_params_list/1,2,3` | `[%{"" => ...}, ...]`          |
| `insert_user_list/1,2,3`              | `[%User{}, ...]`, inserted     |

Insert functions need a repo, a table-backed Ecto schema, and `insert?` not `false`. Embedded
schemas get no insert functions.

### Non-struct factory (`deffactory payload(params \\ %{})`)

| Function              | Returns                   |
| --------------------- | ------------------------- |
| `build_payload/0,1,2` | Whatever the body returns |
| `build_payload_list/1,2,3` | A list of them       |

### Variant (`defvariant admin(...), for: :user`)

| Function                    | Notes                              |
| --------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| `build_admin_user_struct/0,1,2` | `as: :boss` renames to `build_boss_struct` |
| `insert_admin_user/0,1,2`   | Inserts through the base pipeline  |

Every function of the base factory has a variant counterpart.

### Which function?

| Need                                        | Use                  |
| ------------------------------------------- | -------------------- |
| A changeset or function that expects a map  | `build_*_params`     |
| Controller or JSON input                    | `build_*_string_params` |
| A struct to nest in another, no DB row      | `build_*_struct`     |
| A row a query, constraint, or FK needs      | `insert_*`           |
| Insert a struct you edited, with hooks      | `insert_*_struct`    |

## Options
{: .col-2}

### `use FactoryMan`

| Option     | Meaning                                    |
| ---------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| `:repo`    | Ecto repo for inserts                      |
| `:extends` | Parent factory module to inherit from      |
| `:hooks`   | Hooks for every factory in the module      |
| `:strict`  | Default `:strict` for the module           |
| `:body`    | Default `:body` for the module             |

### `deffactory`

| Option     | Meaning                                              |
| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| `:struct`  | Struct or Ecto schema to build                       |
| `:assocs`  | Association builders (Ecto schemas only)             |
| `:strict`  | `true`, `false`, or `[allow: [keys]]`                |
| `:body`    | `:params` (default) or `:struct`                     |
| `:hooks`   | Chained with the module's hooks                      |
| `:repo`    | Overrides the module's repo                          |
| `:insert?` | `false` skips insert functions                       |

### `defvariant`

| Option     | Meaning                                              |
| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| `:for`     | The base factory (required, must be a factory)       |
| `:extends` | Variants of the same factory to build on             |
| `:as`      | Name for the generated functions                     |
| `:assocs`  | Association builders, resolved before the variant body |

### Function options

| Function         | Options                                           |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| `build_*`        | `variants: [...]` only                            |
| `insert_*`       | `variants: [...]`; every other option goes to `Repo.insert!/2` |
| `insert_*_struct`| Repo options only                                 |

## Variants
{: .col-2}

### Precedence (defaults form: `Map.merge(defaults, params)`)

| Wins over               | Example                                        |
| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| Caller over variants    | `build_user_struct(%{role: "owner"}, variants: [:admin])` → `"owner"` |
| Later over earlier      | `variants: [:admin, :moderator]` → `"moderator"` |
| Variant over what it extends | `extends: [:admin]`, whatever the list order |

A variant written `Map.merge(params, forced)` forces its values: it wins over the caller and over
every variant after it in the list.

### Rules

| Rule                | Detail                                           |
| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| Names               | List variants by their `defvariant` name (`:admin`) |
| Own functions       | `build_admin_user_struct(p, variants: [:x])` = `build_user_struct(p, variants: [:admin, :x])` |
| Execution order     | From the last variant to the base factory        |
| Duplicates          | Each variant is applied once, at its first position |
| Definition order    | A variant is defined after the variants it extends |
| Introspection       | `__factory_man__(:variants, :user)`              |

## Strict params
{: .col-2}

### `strict: true` checks

| Check                     | When                           | Catches                          |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------- |
| Unknown keys              | Before hooks and the body      | `%{usernme: "x"}`                |
| Ignored or changed params | After the body and lazy values | A body that forgets its merge    |

### What the second check compares

| Value given              | Kept when                                  |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------ |
| Plain map                | Each of its keys is kept (recursively)     |
| Anything else            | The built value is `==` to it              |
| Function (lazy)          | Not checked                                |
| Association key          | Not checked                                |
| Key in `allow:`          | Not checked, by either check               |

## Hooks
{: .col-2}

### Names and stages

| Hook                   | Receives | Runs                             |
| ---------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------- |
| `:before_build_params` | params   | Before `assocs:` and the body    |
| `:after_build_params`  | params   | After the body and the strict check |
| `:before_build_struct` | params   | Before `struct!/2`               |
| `:after_build_struct`  | struct   | After the struct is built        |
| `:before_insert`       | struct   | Before `Repo.insert!/2`          |
| `:after_insert`        | struct   | After the insert                 |

`body: :struct` skips the three params-stage hooks.

### Forms and placements

| Value                              | Meaning                                  |
| ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| `&M.hook/1`                        | One remote capture                       |
| `[&M.a/1, &M.b/1]`                 | Several, run in order                    |
| `{hooks, :before_parent}`          | Before the inherited hooks (default for `after_*`) |
| `{hooks, :after_parent}`           | After the inherited hooks (default for `before_*`) |
| `{hooks, :replace_parent}`         | Instead of the inherited hooks           |
| `{[], :replace_parent}`            | Switches off the inherited hooks         |

## Associations (`assocs:`)
{: .col-2}

### Builder forms

| Form                                  | Meaning                                  |
| ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| `&build_user_struct/1`                | Builds an absent key with `%{}`          |
| `fn params, factory_params -> ... end`| Also sees keys declared above it         |
| `{builder, default: nil}`             | An absent key stays `nil`                |
| `{builder, default: [%{...}]}`        | An absent list key is built from params  |
| `{builder, required: true}`           | `nil` raises (singular keys only)        |

### Caller values

| Caller gives       | Singular         | Plural (list)          |
| ------------------ | ---------------- | ---------------------- |
| Key absent         | `default:` (`%{}`) | `default:` (`[]`)    |
| `nil`              | `nil`            | Raises (use `[]`)      |
| Params map         | Built            | Raises                 |
| Struct             | Reused           | Raises                 |
| List               | Raises           | Each item resolved     |

## Sequences and reflection
{: .col-2}

### Sequences

| Call                                               | Values                    |
| -------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |
| `FactoryMan.sequence("user")`                      | `"user0"`, `"user1"`, ... |
| `FactoryMan.sequence(:email, &"u#{&1}@x.com")`     | Formatted counter         |
| `FactoryMan.sequence(:role, ["a", "b"])`           | Cycles through the list   |
| `FactoryMan.sequence(:n, &"#{&1}", start_at: 100)` | Starts at 100             |
| `FactoryMan.Sequence.reset(:email)`                | Resets one (async-safe)   |
| `FactoryMan.Sequence.reset()`                      | Resets all, for every test |

### Reflection

| Call                               | Returns                                  |
| ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| `__factory_man__(:opts)`           | The module's resolved options            |
| `__factory_man__(:opts, :user)`    | A factory's or variant's merged options  |
| `__factory_man__(:factories)`      | Factories and variants (full names)      |
| `__factory_man__(:variants, :user)`| A factory's variant names                |
